The sceptics: disagreement and suspension of judgment (@greek-sceptics: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @greek-schools-life, #source @greek-source-diogenes, #philosophy @greek-plotinus, #ancient-greek-philosophy @greek-plotinus) { r_6KEA1AHWJRDT3ZN8VJQTK06ZFK
**Read:** [Diogenes Laertius, Lives and Opinions](../sources/Lives-and-Opinions-Yonge.lingua#r_2MZ8K8NBGJSS2844MJ7DDGR849), Book IX, the life of Pyrrho and its account of sceptical arguments and ways of living. Identify the passages reporting different views and replies. The life is a later account of the tradition rather than a treatise written by Pyrrho.

**Preparation:** [a report and its historical limits](../foundations/Socrates-and-his-sources.lingua#r_1WAA32AYYPKYVETNZ5JGZ2SHFT). [Meno](../socratic/Meno.lingua#r_6NC59NWAQ6A7YZYBJ3CG12SCTN) supplies a useful comparison about continuing inquiry; read that difficulty alongside if needed.

Distinguish three positions: rejecting a particular claim, asserting that no claim can be known, and withholding assent where competing reasons remain unresolved. They have different commitments. Ask how an argument from disagreement reaches its conclusion and whether a stronger reason on one side could change the result.

**Practice:** choose a disputed interpretation from an earlier dialogue. Present the strongest reasons on each side, describe what further evidence might matter, and explain whether suspending judgment is warranted in this case. Then ask what practical decision still has to be made.

**Check:** explain a sceptical argument, a possible self-application problem, and a response. Compare Socratic admission of ignorance with the position you reconstructed; a resemblance in questioning does not establish that the doctrines are identical.

**Further comparison:** use Book VII's account of Stoic views on knowledge in the same retained volume. Identify the criterion the account proposes and what a sceptical challenge would target.

**Finish:** [A comparative philosophical investigation](../questions/Comparative-investigation.lingua#r_20BK69Q76HJXAGZ5J1T097X29G). **Return:** [Schools of life](Schools-of-life.lingua#r_58ENCWSNQARKCDXEP8FVWY9507) · [Ancient Greek philosophy](../Ancient-Greek-Philosophy.lingua#r_464ZHR7ZYC234A0XX2QEW47VB3).
